WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.675
Why does Google Cloud need
a module about a gap?

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:04.275
Because of two facts.

3
00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:08.684
First, Personalized Service Health's
event category has one value,

4
00:00:08.684 --> 00:00:12.050
incident, meaning a service
outage or degradation.

5
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.975
Planned maintenance isn't in it,
and neither are security notices.

6
00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:19.209
Those reach a Google Cloud
project by other channels,

7
00:00:19.209 --> 00:00:22.075
such as the contacts set
in Essential Contacts.

8
00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:29.265
Second, Assured Workloads' supported-products
page lists Personalized Service Health

9
00:00:29.265 --> 00:00:35.175
under twenty-five regional packages,
including US Data Boundary, but not

10
00:00:35.175 --> 00:00:40.100
under FedRAMP Moderate, FedRAMP High, I
L 2, I L 4, I L 5, C J I S or I T A R.

11
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.535
A workload in one of those packages has no

12
00:00:42.535 --> 00:00:45.113
Personalized Service
Health to read at all.

13
00:00:45.113 --> 00:00:49.212
Both gaps share a danger: an
empty list looks like good news.

14
00:00:49.212 --> 00:00:52.382
So this gate collects
what Google publishes,

15
00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:55.700
and writes down, with the
ISSO, what can't arrive.
